1. Definitions

1.1 "Software" means the HostPanel web hosting control panel in object and source form, including all files distributed by Licensor, its command-line tools, daemons, agents, APIs, templates, and Documentation, together with any Updates supplied under this Agreement.

1.2 "Modules" means the billing-system integrations (including but not limited to WHMCS, Blesta, and ClientExec modules), whether distributed with the Software or separately, except to the extent any such module is accompanied by its own license file, in which case that license governs that module.

1.3 "Documentation" means the installation, administration, and API documentation supplied by Licensor.

1.4 "Licensed Server" means a single physical machine, virtual machine, or container instance on which the Software is installed and which is bound to a valid License Key.

1.5 "License Key" means the unique credential issued by Licensor that activates the Software on a Licensed Server for the duration of a Subscription Term.

1.6 "Subscription Term" means the period for which Licensee has paid the applicable Fees, as stated in the applicable order or invoice, including any renewal periods.

1.7 "Licensing Service" means the Licensor-operated service at [hostpanel.online] or its successor endpoints, against which the Software validates License Keys.

1.8 "End Users" means Licensee's own customers or personnel who access hosting accounts administered through the Software, without themselves receiving a copy of the Software.

1.9 "Updates" means bug fixes, patches, security releases, and new versions of the Software that Licensor makes generally available to subscribers at no additional charge.

1.10 "Third-Party Components" means software not authored by Licensor that is distributed with or required by the Software, as identified in the THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES file.

